# The one check in this repository that reads a source instead of a second
# implementation. Every FRI and duplex bound the signature declares is
# recomputed from the cited paper over exact fractions, by arithmetic this
# file owns, and compared. Two implementations of the same reading can share a
# misreading; a second reading of the source cannot be talked into one.
#
# Its history is the reason it exists: it is what caught a rate-convention
# misreading that understated a bound by up to 2.8x. The concrete FRI formulas
# it covers are where the repository's error record is concentrated and where
# mechanization arrives last.

# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/fri_soundcalc.py %zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: soundcalc: every theorem-derived bound matches the declared bound
